; Prove with deeply embedded modal logic
;
; Modal formulas are object terms. `⊢ A` is the Boolean Kurt judgment saying
; that the object formula A is a theorem. This separation makes necessitation
; expressible as an ordinary Kurt rule.

load modal-deep

const P, Q
formula P, Q

; The implicational K axiom is an object-level theorem.

⊢ (P → (Q → P))

; Necessitation turns an object theorem into its boxed theorem.

⊢ □(P → (Q → P))

; Prefix theoremhood and the empty-context sequent notation are connected by
; explicit rules in modal-deep.kurt.

empty ⊢ □(P → (Q → P))

; Modus ponens also lives at the Kurt meta level. First instantiate the
; implication axiom with the theorem above as its antecedent, then apply it.

⊢ ((P → (Q → P)) → (Q → (P → (Q → P))))
⊢ (Q → (P → (Q → P)))
